<title>USA: U.S. growth fund purchases drop - Schwab.</title>
<headline>U.S. growth fund purchases drop - Schwab.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Charles Schwab Corp said customer purchases of U.S. domestic growth mutual funds dropped to $358 million in October, compared to $1.037 billion in September.</p>
<p>Purchases of international growth funds climbed to $188.1 million from $174.3 million.</p>
<p>Balanced funds dropped to $98.1 million from $209 million.</p>
<p>Taxable bond funds were up to $107.6 million from $90.5 million.</p>
<p>Meanwhile sales of tax-advantaged funds increased to $11.9 million from $8.1 million.</p>
</text>
